'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  ch01-first-blink.spin2
''   Purpose....  Your first cog of your own - Spin2 launches a DAT block
''                of PASM2 and then gets out of its way
''   Manual.....  DeSilva PASM2 Tutorial Manual
''   Version....  v3.0.6 (2026-08-16)
''   Appears in.  Chapter 1: Your First Spin -- What's Really Happening
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Jun 2026
''   Updated....  Jul 2026
''
''   This file is an EXAMPLE from the manual above. Everything below
''   this header is byte-identical to the listing printed there --
''   what you read in the manual is what builds here.
''
'' ===========================================================================

CON
  _clkfreq = 200_000_000  ' 200 MHz system clock

PUB main()
    coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @blink_code, 0)  ' Start PASM2 in new cog
    repeat  ' Keep the main cog alive

DAT
        org     0
blink_code
        drvh    #56
        waitx   ##50_000_000
        drvl    #56
        waitx   ##50_000_000
        jmp     #$-6

